  Kaigāru ‘1. old name for the central part of Porangana:du, essentially a region SW of Kotagiri, mainly inhabited by Gaudas and Toreyas; originally it marked the limits of Kurumba territory in the eastern part of the plateau, being bounded by a line from Go:pediṭṭu to Baraliya:r along the NE, another between De:na:yi and De:pa:nu along the NW, then a line from Mu:ku Beṭṭa to Hubbatale in the SW, while the Coonoor R. from there to Baraḷiya:r marked the S boundary of the territory , 2. name of one of the seven maximal lineages making up Maduve clan in Poranga:du and elsewhere’ noun proper-noun uncertain alternate   IDs=f_s7ph7wms4uhu4 SRC=hockings-pilotraichoor1992[p. 116, col. 1]
